{"schema":"reviewgraphen.benchmark.candidate_output.v1","trial_id":"m7-real:snapshot-34:full_review_graphen:2","outcome":"structured","findings":[{"local_id":"predictable-literate-temp-overwrite","locations":[{"path":"rust/fslc/src/main.rs","start_line":37,"end_line":40},{"path":"rust/fslc/src/main.rs","start_line":43,"end_line":68}],"mechanism_tags":["check_write_gap","repeatable_entry","repeated_effect","unstable_token"],"rationale":"Literate materialization uses only the source stem and process ID, then fs::write truncates any existing file at that predictable path and Drop unconditionally removes it. Re-entry in one process aliases the same file, and an unrelated pre-existing file can be overwritten and deleted; it also unnecessarily requires the source directory to be writable.","severity":"medium"},{"local_id":"partial-init-root-misclassified","locations":[{"path":"rust/fsl-runtime/src/explicit.rs","start_line":390,"end_line":398}],"mechanism_tags":["check_write_gap","cross_file_contract","state_transition_gap"],"rationale":"The helper records only whether an init statement touched a root. A write to one map key or one nested struct field therefore removes the entire root from the unassigned result even though other required components remain unwritten, violating the component-level definite-assignment contract.","severity":"medium"}],"obligation_results":[{"packet_id":"context-envelope:sha256:5d648c0c4c1450b5a52fe8a391780ba0f1e0b6115a8f54b279a897faf74efa99","disposition":"issue_present","finding_local_ids":["predictable-literate-temp-overwrite"]},{"packet_id":"context-envelope:sha256:715cf0ca0e59f5cb9ca5281e0b4ce978a435a63b3e806d7c43540a081e0d42ec","disposition":"inconclusive","finding_local_ids":[]},{"packet_id":"context-envelope:sha256:931f3ba29b6941842d8ce0dde7977534a8d18f63e30dbbd96249d5f771971973","disposition":"issue_present","finding_local_ids":["partial-init-root-misclassified"]},{"packet_id":"context-envelope:sha256:ca264117c529d13d74bad07f1fb64ab972